## ADDRNEW

Creates a new address book entry below the current entry.

Syntax: ADDRNEW [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [TYPE] [ALIAS] [NAME] [EMAIL]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  TYPE       Entry type: G=Group, L=Mailing list, omit=Person
  ALIAS      Alias for the new entry
  NAME       Full name
  EMAIL      Email address

At least one of ALIAS, NAME, or EMAIL must be specified.

Return: ALIAS of the created entry in RESULT.

Examples:
  'ADDRNEW ALIAS "jd" NAME "John Doe" EMAIL "john@example.com"'
  'ADDRNEW TYPE G ALIAS "Friends" NAME "Friends Group"'
  'ADDRNEW TYPE L ALIAS "team" NAME "Team List" EMAIL "team@example.com"'

## ADDREDIT

Edits the fields of the current address book entry.
Use ADDRGOTO first to select the entry.

Syntax: ADDREDIT [ALIAS] [NAME] [EMAIL] [PGP] [HOMEPAGE] [STREET] [CITY]
                 [COUNTRY] [PHONE] [COMMENT] [BIRTHDATE/N] [IMAGE]
                 [MEMBER/M] [ADD/S]

Parameters:
  ALIAS        Change alias
  NAME         Full name
  EMAIL        Email address
  PGP          PGP key ID
  HOMEPAGE     Homepage URL
  STREET       Street address
  CITY         City
  COUNTRY      Country
  PHONE        Phone number
  COMMENT      Comment text
  BIRTHDATE/N  Birth date in format DDMMYYYY (e.g. 13091969)
  IMAGE        Path to portrait image file
  MEMBER/M     Member list (for mailing lists only)
  ADD/S        Add members instead of replacing the list

Examples:
  'ADDRGOTO "jd"'
  'ADDREDIT PHONE "+49 123 456" CITY "Berlin" COUNTRY "Germany"'

  /* Add members to a mailing list */
  'ADDRGOTO "team"'
  'ADDREDIT MEMBER "alice" "bob" ADD'

## ADDRDELETE

Deletes an address book entry.

Syntax: ADDRDELETE [ALIAS]

Parameters:
  ALIAS    Alias of the entry to delete. If omitted, the current entry is deleted.

Examples:
  'ADDRDELETE "jd"'
  'ADDRDELETE'

## ADDRGOTO

Makes the specified entry the current one in the address book.

Syntax: ADDRGOTO ALIAS/A

Parameters:
  ALIAS/A    Alias of the entry (required)

Example:
  'ADDRGOTO "jd"'

## ADDRINFO

Returns information about an address book entry.

Syntax: ADDRINFO [VAR/K] [STEM/K] ALIAS/A

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  ALIAS/A    Alias of the entry (required)

Return fields:
  TYPE       P=Person, L=Mailing list, G=Group
  NAME       Full name
  EMAIL      Email address
  PGP        PGP key ID
  HOMEPAGE   Homepage URL
  STREET     Street address
  CITY       City
  COUNTRY    Country
  PHONE      Phone number
  COMMENT    Comment
  BIRTHDATE  Date in format YYYYMMDD
  IMAGE      File path of portrait image
  MEMBERS    Members of a mailing list

Examples:
  'ADDRINFO STEM ai. "jd"'
  SAY "Name:" ai.name
  SAY "Email:" ai.email
  SAY "Type:" ai.type

## ADDRFIND

Searches the address book for matching entries.

Syntax: ADDRFIND [VAR/K] [STEM/K] PATTERN/A [NAMEONLY/S] [EMAILONLY/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K        Store result in named variable
  STEM/K       Store result in stem variable
  PATTERN/A    Search term (required)
  NAMEONLY/S   Search only in the "Full name" field
  EMAILONLY/S  Search only in the "Address" field

Return: ALIAS/M (list of matching aliases)

Examples:
  'ADDRFIND STEM res. "example.com" EMAILONLY'
  DO i = 0 TO res.alias.count - 1
      SAY res.alias.i
  END

  'ADDRFIND STEM res. "Marcel Beck" NAMEONLY'

## ADDRRESOLVE

Resolves an alias or name to email address(es).

Syntax: ADDRRESOLVE [VAR/K] [STEM/K] ALIAS/A

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  ALIAS/A    Alias or name to resolve (required)

Return: EMAIL/M (list of email addresses)

Example:
  'ADDRRESOLVE STEM res. "team"'
  DO i = 0 TO res.email.count - 1
      SAY res.email.i
  END

## ADDRLOAD

Loads an address book from a file.

Syntax: ADDRLOAD FILENAME/A

Parameters:
  FILENAME/A    Path to the address book file (required)

Example:
  'ADDRLOAD "PROGDIR:.addressbook"'

## ADDRSAVE

Saves the address book to a file.

Syntax: ADDRSAVE [FILENAME]

Parameters:
  FILENAME    Path to save to. If omitted, the current file is used.

Examples:
  'ADDRSAVE'
  'ADDRSAVE "RAM:addressbook_backup"'

## SETFOLDER

Switches to a mailbox/folder.

Syntax: SETFOLDER FOLDER/A

Parameters:
  FOLDER/A    Folder name or number (required)
              0=Inbox is always the first folder

Examples:
  'SETFOLDER "Eingang"'
  'SETFOLDER 0'
  'SETFOLDER "Sent"'

## FOLDERINFO

Returns information about a mailbox/folder.

Syntax: FOLDERINFO [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [FOLDER]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  FOLDER     Folder name or number. If omitted, uses current folder.

Return fields:
  NUMBER/N   Internal number (0=Inbox)
  NAME       Display name
  PATH       Directory name
  TOTAL/N    Total number of messages
  NEW/N      Number of new messages
  UNREAD/N   Number of unread messages
  SIZE/N     Size in bytes
  TYPE/N     Folder type:
             0=normal, 1=Inbox, 2=Outbox, 3=Sent (default),
             4=Deleted, 5=Sent+Received, 6=Sent

Examples:
  'FOLDERINFO STEM fi.'
  SAY "Mailbox:" fi.name "—" fi.total "messages," fi.new "new"

  'FOLDERINFO STEM fi. "Outbox"'

## NEWMAILFILE

Returns an unused filename for a new message in a folder.

Syntax: NEWMAILFILE [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [FOLDER]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  FOLDER     Folder name or number. If omitted, uses current folder.

Return: FILENAME

Example:
  'NEWMAILFILE STEM nf.'
  SAY "New file:" nf.filename

## SETMAIL

Selects a message in the current mailbox by position index.

Syntax: SETMAIL NUM/N/A

Parameters:
  NUM/N/A    0-based message index (required)

Example:
  'SETMAIL 0'
  'SETMAIL 5'

## SETMAILFILE

Selects a message by its filename.

Syntax: SETMAILFILE MAILFILE/A

Parameters:
  MAILFILE/A    Filename of the message (required)

Example:
  'SETMAILFILE "000001.001"'

## LISTSELECT

Selects or deselects messages in the current mailbox.

Syntax: LISTSELECT MODE/A

Parameters:
  MODE/A     Selection mode (required)
             N = Select none (clear selection)
             A = Select all
             T = Toggle selection
             numeric = Add message at position to selection

Examples:
  'LISTSELECT A'
  'LISTSELECT N'
  'LISTSELECT 5'

## GETSELECTED

Returns the positions of the selected messages.

Syntax: GETSELECTED [VAR/K] [STEM/K]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable

Return: NUM/N/M (list of selected message positions)

Example:
  'GETSELECTED STEM sel.'
  DO i = 0 TO sel.num.count - 1
      SAY "Selected:" sel.num.i
  END

## MAILINFO

Returns detailed information about a message.

Syntax: MAILINFO [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [INDEX/N]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  INDEX/N    Message index (0-based). If omitted, uses current message.

Return fields:
  INDEX/N    Message index
  STATUS     Message status:
             N=new, O=read, U=unread, R=replied,
             F=forwarded, S=sent, W=waiting, H=hold, E=error
  FROM       Sender
  TO         Recipient
  REPLYTO    Reply-to address
  SUBJECT    Subject
  FILENAME   File path of the message
  SIZE/N     Size in bytes
  DATE       Date string
  FLAGS      8-byte string "MARCS-00":
             M=Multipart, A=Attachments, R=Report,
             C=Crypted (encrypted), S=Signed,
             last two digits=user flags (see SETFLAG)
  MSGID/N    32-bit compressed message ID

Examples:
  'MAILINFO STEM mi. 0'
  SAY "From:" mi.from
  SAY "Subject:" mi.subject
  SAY "Status:" mi.status
  SAY "Size:" mi.size "bytes"

  /* Check for attachments */
  'MAILINFO STEM mi.'
  IF SUBSTR(mi.flags, 2, 1) = 'A' THEN SAY "Has attachments"

## MAILREAD

Opens the current message in a read window.

Syntax: MAILREAD [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [WINDOW/N] [QUIET/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  WINDOW/N   Activate an already open read window by number
  QUIET/S    Open window invisibly (hidden)

Return: WINDOW/N (read window number)

Example:
  'MAILREAD'
  window = RESULT

  'MAILREAD QUIET'

## MAILREPLY

Opens a compose window to reply to the selected message.

Syntax: MAILREPLY [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [QUIET/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  QUIET/S    Open window invisibly

Return: WINDOW/N (compose window number)

Example:
  'MAILREPLY QUIET'

## MAILFORWARD

Opens a compose window to forward the selected message.

Syntax: MAILFORWARD [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [QUIET/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  QUIET/S    Open window invisibly

Return: WINDOW/N (compose window number)

Example:
  'MAILFORWARD QUIET'

## MAILBOUNCE

Opens a compose window to redirect (bounce) the selected message.
The message is resent with modified headers.

Syntax: MAILBOUNCE [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [QUIET/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  QUIET/S    Open window invisibly

Return: WINDOW/N (compose window number)

Example:
  'MAILBOUNCE QUIET'

## MAILEDIT

Opens the selected message for editing.

Syntax: MAILEDIT [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [QUIET/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  QUIET/S    Open window invisibly

Return: WINDOW/N (edit window number)

Example:
  'MAILEDIT'

## MAILCOPY

Copies the selected messages to another mailbox.

Syntax: MAILCOPY FOLDER/A

Parameters:
  FOLDER/A    Destination folder name or number (required)

Example:
  'MAILCOPY "Archive"'
  'MAILCOPY 3'

## MAILMOVE

Moves the selected messages to another mailbox.

Syntax: MAILMOVE FOLDER/A

Parameters:
  FOLDER/A    Destination folder name or number (required)

Example:
  'MAILMOVE "Archive"'

## MAILDELETE

Deletes the selected messages.

Syntax: MAILDELETE [ATONCE/S] [FORCE/S]

Parameters:
  ATONCE/S    Delete immediately (skip trash folder)
  FORCE/S     No confirmation prompt

Examples:
  'MAILDELETE'
  'MAILDELETE ATONCE FORCE'

## MAILSTATUS

Changes the status of the selected messages.

Syntax: MAILSTATUS STATUS

Parameters:
  STATUS     New status:
             O = Read (Old)
             U = Unread
             H = Hold
             W = Ready to send (Waiting)

Examples:
  'MAILSTATUS O'
  'MAILSTATUS U'
  'MAILSTATUS H'

## MAILCHANGESUBJECT

Changes the subject of the selected message(s).

Syntax: MAILCHANGESUBJECT SUBJECT/A

Parameters:
  SUBJECT/A    New subject text (required)

Example:
  'MAILCHANGESUBJECT "Updated Subject"'

## MAILSEND

Sends selected or all messages in the outbox.

Syntax: MAILSEND [ALL/S]

Parameters:
  ALL/S    Send all messages in outbox (not just selected)

Examples:
  'MAILSEND'
  'MAILSEND ALL'

## MAILSENDALL

Sends all messages in the outbox.

Syntax: MAILSENDALL

Example:
  'MAILSENDALL'

## MAILFILTER

Filters messages in the current mailbox using configured filter rules.

Syntax: MAILFILTER [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [ALL/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  ALL/S      Filter all messages. Without ALL, only new messages are filtered.

Return fields:
  CHECKED/N     Number of messages checked
  BOUNCED/N     Number bounced
  FORWARDED/N   Number forwarded
  REPLIED/N     Number auto-replied
  EXECUTED/N    Number that triggered script execution
  MOVED/N       Number moved
  DELETED/N     Number deleted

Example:
  'MAILFILTER STEM mf. ALL'
  SAY "Checked:" mf.checked "Moved:" mf.moved "Deleted:" mf.deleted

## MAILUPDATE

Refreshes/rebuilds the index of the current mailbox.

Syntax: MAILUPDATE

Example:
  'MAILUPDATE'

## MAILEXPORT

Exports messages to a file.

Syntax: MAILEXPORT FILENAME/A [ALL/S] [APPEND/S]

Parameters:
  FILENAME/A    Output file path (required)
  ALL/S         Export all messages (not just selected)
  APPEND/S      Append to existing file instead of overwriting

Examples:
  'MAILEXPORT "RAM:messages.txt"'
  'MAILEXPORT "RAM:messages.txt" ALL APPEND'

## MAILIMPORT

Imports messages from a file into the current folder.

Syntax: MAILIMPORT FILENAME/A [WAIT/S]

Parameters:
  FILENAME/A    Input file path (required)
  WAIT/S        Let user make a pre-selection before importing

Examples:
  'MAILIMPORT "RAM:messages.txt"'
  'MAILIMPORT "RAM:messages.txt" WAIT'

## SETFLAG

Sets user-definable flags on the current message.

Syntax: SETFLAG [VOL/K/N] [PER/K/N]

Parameters:
  VOL/K/N    Volatile flag (lost on restart), values 0-7
  PER/K/N    Permanent flag (stored in file comment), values 0-7

The flags appear as the last two digits in the FLAGS field of MAILINFO.

Examples:
  'SETFLAG VOL 1'
  'SETFLAG PER 3'
  'SETFLAG VOL 0 PER 0'

## MAILCHECK

Checks for new emails and downloads them.

Syntax: MAILCHECK [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [POP/K/N] [MANUAL/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  POP/K/N    Query only a specific POP3 server by number
  MANUAL/S   Let user pre-select which messages to download

Return fields:
  DOWNLOADED/N   Number of messages downloaded
  ONSERVER/N     Number of messages still on server
  DUPSKIPPED/N   Number of duplicates skipped
  DELETED/N      Number deleted from server

Examples:
  'MAILCHECK STEM mc.'
  SAY mc.downloaded "new messages downloaded"
  SAY mc.onserver "on server"

  'MAILCHECK POP 0'

## READCLOSE

Closes the active read window.

Syntax: READCLOSE

Example:
  'READCLOSE'

## READINFO

Returns information about the attachments of the message in the
active read window.

Syntax: READINFO [VAR/K] [STEM/K]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable

Return fields (all /M = multiple):
  FILENAME/M    Original filenames of attachments
  FILETYPE/M    MIME types of attachments
  FILESIZE/N/M  Sizes in bytes
  TEMPFILE/M    Temporary file paths (for decoded attachments)

Example:
  'READINFO STEM ri.'
  DO i = 0 TO ri.filename.count - 1
      SAY "Attachment:" ri.filename.i "(" ri.filetype.i "," ri.filesize.i "bytes)"
  END

## READPRINT

Prints a message or a specific attachment from the read window.

Syntax: READPRINT [PART/N]

Parameters:
  PART/N    Attachment number to print. If omitted, prints the visible message.

Examples:
  'READPRINT'
  'READPRINT 1'

## READSAVE

Saves a message or a specific attachment from the read window to a file.

Syntax: READSAVE [PART/N] [FILENAME/K] [OVERWRITE/S]

Parameters:
  PART/N        Attachment number to save. If omitted, saves the message.
  FILENAME/K    Destination file path. If omitted, a file requester appears.
  OVERWRITE/S   Overwrite existing file without asking

Examples:
  'READSAVE FILENAME "RAM:message.txt"'
  'READSAVE PART 1 FILENAME "RAM:attachment.pdf" OVERWRITE'

## MAILWRITE

Opens a new compose window for writing a message.

Syntax: MAILWRITE [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [WINDOW/N] [QUIET/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  WINDOW/N   Activate an already open compose window by number
  QUIET/S    Open window invisibly (hidden)

Return: WINDOW/N (compose window number)

Examples:
  'MAILWRITE'
  window = RESULT

  'MAILWRITE QUIET'

## WRITETO

Sets the "To" field in the active compose window.

Syntax: WRITETO ADDRESS/A/M [ADD/S]

Parameters:
  ADDRESS/A/M    Email address(es) (required, multiple allowed)
  ADD/S          Append to existing addresses instead of replacing

Examples:
  'WRITETO "user@example.com"'
  'WRITETO "alice@example.com" "bob@example.com"'
  'WRITETO "cc@example.com" ADD'

## WRITECC

Sets the "CC" (carbon copy) field in the active compose window.

Syntax: WRITECC ADDRESS/A/M [ADD/S]

Parameters:
  ADDRESS/A/M    Email address(es) (required, multiple allowed)
  ADD/S          Append to existing addresses instead of replacing

Examples:
  'WRITECC "manager@example.com"'
  'WRITECC "team@example.com" ADD'

## WRITEBCC

Sets the "BCC" (blind carbon copy) field in the active compose window.

Syntax: WRITEBCC ADDRESS/A/M [ADD/S]

Parameters:
  ADDRESS/A/M    Email address(es) (required, multiple allowed)
  ADD/S          Append to existing addresses instead of replacing

Example:
  'WRITEBCC "archive@example.com"'

## WRITEMAILTO

Sets the "To" field, replacing all existing addresses.

Syntax: WRITEMAILTO ADDRESS/A/M

Parameters:
  ADDRESS/A/M    Email address(es) (required, multiple allowed)

Example:
  'WRITEMAILTO "newrecipient@example.com"'

## WRITEFROM

Sets the "From" field in the active compose window.

Syntax: WRITEFROM ADDRESS/A

Parameters:
  ADDRESS/A    Email address (required)

Example:
  'WRITEFROM "sender@example.com"'

## WRITEREPLYTO

Sets the "Reply-To" field in the active compose window.

Syntax: WRITEREPLYTO ADDRESS/A

Parameters:
  ADDRESS/A    Reply-to email address (required)

Example:
  'WRITEREPLYTO "replies@example.com"'

## WRITESUBJECT

Sets the subject in the active compose window.

Syntax: WRITESUBJECT SUBJECT/A

Parameters:
  SUBJECT/A    Subject text (required). Strings with spaces must be quoted.

Examples:
  'WRITESUBJECT "Monthly Report"'
  'WRITESUBJECT "Re: Your question"'

## WRITEATTACH

Adds a file as an attachment to the message.

Syntax: WRITEATTACH FILE/A [DESC] [ENCMODE] [CTYPE]

Parameters:
  FILE/A     File path (required)
  DESC       Description of the attachment
  ENCMODE    Encoding mode:
             uu  = UUencode
             b64 = Base64 (recommended)
  CTYPE      MIME Content-Type (e.g. "image/jpeg", "application/pdf")

Examples:
  'WRITEATTACH "WORK:Bilder/foto.jpg" DESC "Vacation photo" ENCMODE b64 CTYPE "image/jpeg"'
  'WRITEATTACH "Work:Reports/March.pdf" "Monthly report" b64'

## WRITEOPTIONS

Sets options for the message being composed.

Syntax: WRITEOPTIONS [DELETE/S] [RECEIPT/S] [NOTIF/S] [ADDINFO/S]
                     [IMPORTANCE/N] [SIG/N] [SECURITY/N]

Parameters:
  DELETE/S       Delete message after sending
  RECEIPT/S      Request read receipt
  NOTIF/S        Request message notification (tracking)
  ADDINFO/S      Add personal information to headers
  IMPORTANCE/N   Priority level:
                 0 = High
                 1 = Normal
                 2 = Low
  SIG/N          Signature to use:
                 0 = None
                 1 = Signature 1
                 2 = Signature 2
                 3 = Signature 3
  SECURITY/N     Security level:
                 0 = Normal (no encryption)
                 1-5 = Security levels

Examples:
  'WRITEOPTIONS IMPORTANCE 0 RECEIPT'
  'WRITEOPTIONS SIG 1 SECURITY 0'

## WRITEEDITOR

Passes an ARexx command to the internal TextEditor (TextEditor.mcc)
that controls the mail body editor.

Syntax: WRITEEDITOR COMMAND/A

Parameters:
  COMMAND/A    TextEditor.mcc ARexx command (required)

Available TextEditor.mcc commands:

Clipboard & Editing:
  CLEAR        Clear all editor contents
  CUT          Cut selected text to clipboard
  COPY         Copy selected text to clipboard
  PASTE        Paste from clipboard at cursor
  ERASE        Erase selected text (no clipboard)
  DELETE       Delete character at cursor
  BACKSPACE    Delete character before cursor
  KILLLINE     Delete entire current line
  UNDO         Undo last action
  REDO         Redo last undone action

Navigation:
  GOTOLINE /N/A       Go to line number
  GOTOCOLUMN /N/A     Go to column number
  CURSOR Up/Down/Left/Right   Move cursor one step
  NEXT Word/Sentence/Paragraph/Page     Move forward
  PREVIOUS Word/Sentence/Paragraph/Page Move backward
  POSITION SOF/EOF/SOL/EOL/SOW/EOW/SOV/EOV  Jump to position

Position codes:
  SOF = Start Of File    EOF = End Of File
  SOL = Start Of Line    EOL = End Of Line
  SOW = Start Of Word    EOW = End Of Word
  SOV = Start Of View    EOV = End Of View

Bookmarks:
  SETBOOKMARK /N/A     Set bookmark (1-3)
  GOTOBOOKMARK /N/A    Jump to bookmark (1-3)

Text & Query:
  TEXT /F              Insert text at cursor (*n for newline)
  GETLINE              Get current line text (returns RESULT)
  LINE /N/A            Get/set current line number (returns RESULT)
  COLUMN /N/A          Get/set current column (returns RESULT)
  GETCURSOR Line/Column  Get cursor position (returns RESULT)

Selection:
  MARK On/Off          Start or stop text selection
  TOUPPER              Convert selected text to uppercase
  TOLOWER              Convert selected text to lowercase

Examples:
  /* Insert text */
  'WRITEEDITOR "TEXT Hello World"'

  /* Insert multi-line text (use *n for newline) */
  'WRITEEDITOR "TEXT Hi,*n"'
  'WRITEEDITOR "TEXT *n"'
  'WRITEEDITOR "TEXT Here is the report.*n"'

  /* Go to beginning of file */
  'WRITEEDITOR "POSITION SOF"'

  /* Go to line 10, column 5 */
  'WRITEEDITOR "GOTOLINE 10"'
  'WRITEEDITOR "GOTOCOLUMN 5"'

  /* Select and copy a line */
  'WRITEEDITOR "POSITION SOL"'
  'WRITEEDITOR "MARK ON"'
  'WRITEEDITOR "POSITION EOL"'
  'WRITEEDITOR "COPY"'
  'WRITEEDITOR "MARK OFF"'

  /* Get the current line text */
  'WRITEEDITOR "GETLINE"'
  SAY RESULT

  /* Get cursor position */
  'WRITEEDITOR "GETCURSOR Line"'
  line = RESULT
  'WRITEEDITOR "GETCURSOR Column"'
  col = RESULT

## WRITESEND

Sends the message immediately from the active compose window.

Syntax: WRITESEND

Example:
  'WRITESEND'

## WRITEQUEUE

Puts the message in the outbox queue.

Syntax: WRITEQUEUE [HOLD/S]

Parameters:
  HOLD/S    Mark as "hold" — message is not sent automatically

Examples:
  'WRITEQUEUE'
  'WRITEQUEUE HOLD'

## REQUEST

Opens a requester window with freely definable buttons.

Syntax: REQUEST [VAR/K] [STEM/K] BODY/A GADGETS/A

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  BODY/A     Message text (required)
  GADGETS/A  Button labels separated by | (required)

Return: RESULT/N
  0 = Rightmost button (typically Cancel)
  1 = Leftmost button
  2 = Second from left, etc.

Example:
  'REQUEST BODY "Really delete message?" GADGETS "Yes|No|Cancel"'
  IF RESULT = 1 THEN SAY "Yes selected"
  IF RESULT = 2 THEN SAY "No selected"
  IF RESULT = 0 THEN SAY "Cancel selected"

## REQUESTFOLDER

Opens a mailbox/folder selection dialog.

Syntax: REQUESTFOLDER [VAR/K] [STEM/K] BODY/A [EXCLUDEACTIVE/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K              Store result in named variable
  STEM/K             Store result in stem variable
  BODY/A             Prompt text (required)
  EXCLUDEACTIVE/S    Exclude the currently active folder from the list

Return: FOLDER (selected folder name)
RC = 1 if the user cancels.

Example:
  'REQUESTFOLDER BODY "Move messages to:"'
  IF RC = 0 THEN 'MAILMOVE "'RESULT'"'

## REQUESTSTRING

Opens a text input dialog.

Syntax: REQUESTSTRING [VAR/K] [STEM/K] BODY/A [STRING/K] [SECRET/S]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  BODY/A     Prompt text (required)
  STRING/K   Default text for the input field
  SECRET/S   Hide input (for passwords)

Return: STRING (entered text)
RC = 1 if the user cancels.

Examples:
  'REQUESTSTRING BODY "Enter search term:" STRING "default"'
  IF RC = 0 THEN SAY "Entered:" RESULT

  'REQUESTSTRING BODY "Password:" SECRET'

## APPBUSY

Sets YAM into "busy" state. User input is disabled and a status
text is shown.

Syntax: APPBUSY [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [TEXT]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  TEXT       Status text to display

RC = 1 if YAM is already busy.

Note: Always call APPNOBUSY when done!

Example:
  'APPBUSY TEXT "Please wait..."'
  /* ... operations ... */
  'APPNOBUSY'

## APPNOBUSY

Clears the "busy" state of YAM, re-enabling user input.

Syntax: APPNOBUSY

RC = 1 if YAM is still busy (nested busy calls).

Example:
  'APPNOBUSY'

## INFO

Returns program information about YAM.

Syntax: INFO [VAR/K] [STEM/K] [ITEM]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable
  ITEM       Information to retrieve:
             TITLE, AUTHOR, COPYRIGHT, DESCRIPTION,
             VERSION, BASE, SCREEN

Return: VALUE in RESULT

Example:
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'INFO ITEM TITLE'
  SAY RESULT

  'INFO ITEM VERSION'
  SAY RESULT

## USERINFO

Returns information about the currently logged-in user.

Syntax: USERINFO [VAR/K] [STEM/K]

Parameters:
  VAR/K      Store result in named variable
  STEM/K     Store result in stem variable

Return fields:
  USERNAME    Username
  EMAIL       Email address
  REALNAME    Real name
  CONFIG      Configuration file path
  MAILDIR     Mail directory path
  FOLDERS/N   Number of folders

Example:
  'USERINFO STEM ui.'
  SAY "User:" ui.username
  SAY "Email:" ui.email
  SAY "Mailboxes:" ui.folders

## ISONLINE

Checks whether YAM is currently sending or receiving emails.

Syntax: ISONLINE

Return: RC = 1 if YAM is online (sending/receiving), RC = 0 otherwise.

Example:
  'ISONLINE'
  IF RC = 1 THEN SAY "YAM is busy sending/receiving"

## HIDE

Iconifies YAM (minimizes to AppIcon on Workbench).

Syntax: HIDE

Example:
  'HIDE'

## SHOW

Restores YAM from iconified state.

Syntax: SHOW

Example:
  'SHOW'

## SCREENTOFRONT

Brings the YAM screen to the front.

Syntax: SCREENTOFRONT

Example:
  'SCREENTOFRONT'

## SCREENTOBACK

Sends the YAM screen to the back.

Syntax: SCREENTOBACK

Example:
  'SCREENTOBACK'

## HELP

Outputs a list of all supported ARexx commands.

Syntax: HELP [FILE]

Parameters:
  FILE    Output file path. If omitted, output goes to the shell window.

Examples:
  'HELP'
  'HELP FILE "RAM:yam_commands.txt"'

## QUIT

Quits YAM.

Syntax: QUIT [FORCE/S]

Parameters:
  FORCE/S    Skip confirmation prompts

Examples:
  'QUIT'
  'QUIT FORCE'

## GETURL

Downloads a file via HTTP from the internet.

Syntax: GETURL URL/A FILENAME/A

Parameters:
  URL/A         URL to download (required)
  FILENAME/A    Destination file path (required)

Return codes:
  RC = 0    Successful
  RC = 5    No online connection
  RC = 10   URL not found

Example:
  'GETURL "http://example.com/file.txt" "RAM:file.txt"'
  IF RC = 0 THEN SAY "Download successful"
  IF RC = 5 THEN SAY "Not online"
  IF RC = 10 THEN SAY "URL not found"
